  "sharing_rule": "Exact original reference and rendered presentation. Existing external portrait family aliases omit only unused fallback ornaments; project atlases remain strict.",
  "authoring_instructions": "Create a newly articulated 2D isometric RPG animation atlas based strictly on the attached original character. Preserve its exact silhouette, proportions, materials, colors and face; use this original as the character model, never invent another creature. Match the small detailed painted game sprite style and camera. Fully transparent RGBA background, no labels, no grid, no scenery. EXACTLY 8 columns and 13 rows, 104 complete separated poses. Columns always E screen-right profile, SE front-right, S full front, SW front-left, W screen-left profile, NW back-left, N full back, NE back-right. Front shows original chest/face; back shows the back of the head and shoulders, no face. Keep each pose visibly SMALL in its cell, including all extended arms: at most 50 percent of cell width and height, with at least 25 fully transparent pixels around every body and a large outer transparent margin. Never overlap neighboring poses or touch sheet edges. Consistent model scale throughout. EXACT thirteen rows top to bottom: 1 neutral idle; 2 breathing idle, chest rises; 3 locomotion left leg ahead; 4 passing step; 5 locomotion right leg ahead; 6 attack windup, pull one fist back; 7 attack contact, heavy fist fully punches in the facing direction; 8 recovery, retract fist; 9 hit recoil backwards; 10 recovery from hit; 11 death knees buckle; 12 death body falls close to ground; 13 final flat collapsed body. Death remains one connected contiguous body/pile, with arms still connected, no detached flying parts. Every row must contain eight genuine different compass views. Every action row must have actually articulated different arms/legs/torso, never repeated or translated stills. Keep clear empty transparent gutters. No text. This is the original ICE GOLEM, a pale silver-blue crystalline hunched body with transparent-looking jagged ice chunks, massive low swinging arms, small recessed angular head, broad shoulders, short icy legs and large icy fists. Preserve the original cold pale-blue/white highlights and dark-blue cracks, and its exact squat rocklike proportions. No clothes, no weapons, no armor, no horns, no human redesign, no red or gold accents. No detached snowflakes, sparkles, fog, particles or extra ice shards. Keep the ice material on one connected articulated body throughout, including a contiguous collapsed corpse with limbs still attached.",
